course: dictionary
lesson: 3314
title: A sudden discovery
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are cries. «Eureka!» is what you shout when you suddenly find something out or work something out. It means "I have found it!" and it is a shout of joy.
explain: Eureka can also be a noun. A eureka moment is the instant you suddenly understand something or have a great idea. In the story of Archimedes, the water rose as he got into his bath, and he saw how to test a crown. That sudden idea is a eureka moment.
explain: Use the context to check. The words around «eureka» tell you what happened: someone found an answer, had an idea, or understood something at once. Then swap in your meaning, "I have found it!", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Eureka!» means "I have found it!" and is a shout of joy when you suddenly discover something.
fact: A «eureka moment» is the instant you suddenly understand something or have a great idea.
fact: The story says the Greek scientist Archimedes shouted «Eureka!» in his bath, but the story may not be true.
fact: Context clues, like what happens just before or after the word, help you work out its meaning.
exercise: Mia shouted «Eureka!» when she finally solved the puzzle. What does this show? | Tiredness after a long day | Fear of the dark | *Joy at a sudden discovery | Anger at losing the game
exercise: Ben says, «I had a eureka moment in the shower!» What is a eureka moment? | A time when you feel sleepy | *The instant you suddenly understand something or have a great idea | A long wait for the bus | A loud noise in the street
exercise: «Archimedes is said to have shouted "Eureka!", but the story may not be true.» Is the story certainly true? | Yes, it is proved in every science book | It is not a story at all | *No, it may not be true, so it may be a legend | Yes, because it is in a bath
test: Which word means "I have found it!"? | Shh | Ouch | Hooray | *Eureka
test: Which phrase names a sudden idea? | a rainy afternoon | a long queue | *a eureka moment | a sleepy cat
exam: «Eureka!» called Emma, when the answer finally clicked. What does she mean? | She is lost and needs help | *I have found it! | She is going home now | Stop making that noise right now
